artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $A$ be a tensor with one physical index of dimension $d$ and four virtual indices of dimension $D$, and consider the translationally invariant Projected Entangled Pair State (PEPS) $|\Psi_L(A)\rangle$ on an $L\times L$ torus obtained by placing a copy of $A$ at every site of the square lattice and contracting the virtual indices along the edges according to the periodic boundary conditions. For a connected square region $R$ consisting of $k\times k$ sites, let $\mathcal{V}_R \subset (\mathbb{C}^d)^{\otimes |R|}$ be the linear span of all vectors obtainable from the tensor network on $R$ as the open virtual indices on the boundary of $R$ vary over all values, and let $\Pi_R$ be the orthogonal projector onto $\mathcal{V}_R^\perp$. Define the parent Hamiltonian
$$H_L \;=\; \sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_L^2}\, \tau_x(\Pi_R),$$
where $\tau_x$ denotes translation by $x$. 

Determine the weakest possible conditions on the tensor $A$, together with the smallest possible size $k$ of the region $R$, such that the following two properties hold simultaneously for all sufficiently large $L$:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $|\Psi_L(A)\rangle$ is, up to scalars, the unique ground state of $H_L$;
\item there exists a constant $\gamma>0$, independent of $L$, such that the spectral gap of $H_L$ above its ground state energy is at least $\gamma$.
\end{enumerate}
